    "prompt": "16:9 widescreen. High-end cinematic 3D render with feature-animation polish, extreme architectural detail, no plastic sheen. Cool early dawn. [SCALE RULE — the whole point] The architecture is the subject. Each human figure stands no taller than a single balustrade post beside them, roughly one fortieth the height of the hall behind them, and occupies about 3% of the frame height — a few dozen pixels tall. A viewer should scan the image for a moment before noticing that anyone is there at all. Never enlarge them for legibility. [VANTAGE] Camera positioned far back and slightly elevated, a long-lens read at 29 degrees (75mm) that compresses the tiers into stacked planes. [THE ARCHITECTURE] A colossal ceremonial hall crowns the upper center of the frame, seated on nine receding tiers of white jade platform. Its roof ridge stands two hundred meters above the base. Across its front runs a colonnade of monolithic ivory stone columns, each over three meters thick and tens of meters tall, carrying dark vermillion matte-lacquered timber brackets and deep blue-grey tiled eaves. Below, a single vast stairway of more than three hundred treads descends toward camera, flanked the whole way by low carved balustrades with posts at even intervals. Form follows Tang-Song official building canon scaled up rigorously — symmetrical, structurally sound, restrained, no fantasy ornament. [THE FIGURES] Four people are distributed along the stairway at widely separated heights, each alone, each seen from behind as a pale vertical mark in white and celadon robes. The nearest stands at the lower third; the farthest is barely a light speck near the colonnade. Their scale against the stair and the columns is the only information the image gives about how large any of this is. No group, no crowd, no gesture. [SURROUNDINGS] The platform's edges fall away into an unbroken cloud sea that rolls slowly at both sides and behind, its upper surface catching the first light. Dark green gnarled pines cling to the terrace edges at intervals, small against the stonework. Distant subsidiary halls and a far gate-tower recede along the same axis, dissolving into haze. [SKY] Pale blue-grey washing to cool ivory near the horizon. A very large pale moon sits low behind the hall, its diameter about one third of frame height, craters visible, integrated into the air — thin cloud crossing in front of it, a soft glow at its limb, its lower edge softened by haze. [LIGHT] Low cold dawn light from behind camera-left rakes across the stair, throwing long crisp shadows down the treads from every balustrade post — those repeating shadows are the second scale device and must read clearly. Roof ridges and column tops catch a thin warm gold edge; the masses stay in cool blue-grey diffuse light. No god rays, no flare. [ATMOSPHERE] Haze at 40%, building layer by layer with distance so the near stair reads crisp, the colonnade softer, the far gate-tower nearly dissolved. Eight or more depth layers. [COLOR] Ivory white weathered stone, dark vermillion matte lacquer, deep blue-grey tile, dark green pine, pale cool sky. Warm gold only as a thin rim on ridges and column tops, under 5% of the frame. Clean and cool, never muddy, never orange. [RENDER] Physically real materials — mottled weathering on stone, fine crazing in the lacquer, individual roof tiles readable on the near eaves. Low-contrast curve, shadows lifted holding texture, highlights rolled off. Mood: monumental, silent, humbling. [AVOID] Figures rendered larger than a balustrade post, figures near the camera, crowds, faces, birds or cranes, golden-orange grade, plastic surfaces, atmospheric haze so heavy the architecture loses detail, symmetrical dead-center framing without depth cues.",
